                <pb facs="0571" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg491"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 857.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instruction No. 883,
                    of the 5th ultimo, and to previous correspondence respecting the case of J. L.
                    Molloy, a prisoner of war in Bermuda, I have the honor to state that upon
                    information received from Lord Lansdowne the general officer commanding at
                    Bermuda has been requested by telegraph to allow the United States consul at
                    Hamilton to interview Molloy and to obtain an affidavit from him.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
